{
  "name": "en-rules-v1",
  "description": "Generative English morphology rules learned by induction, stored on the field as conditioned clause edges, and verified by the held-out gate (generalisation + negative control + ablation). Each rule is a list of [base, inflected] pairs; the learner induces a class-conditioned decision list (e.g. consonant+y -> -ies, sibilant -> -es, else -> -s) using only the vowel set as a primitive, and applies it to never-taught words. +s is the elsewhere/default class, matching natural frequency.",
